conbody.p:
In the CSS style sheet applied to this HTML, the flagging could be styled in a variety of ways. Here the CSS adds different icons before the paragraphs and sets their background colors to different values. Modern browsers should
            automatically make the details element expandable.
/* Style for flagged content */

@font-face {
  font-family: "Font Awesome";
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 900;
  src: url("https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.0/webfonts/fa-solid-900.woff2") format("woff2"),
       url("https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.0/webfonts/fa-solid-900.woff") format("woff");
}    
:root {
  font-family: sans-serif;
}

p.flag-novice {
  background-color: aqua;
}
p.flag-novice:before {
   font-family: 'Font Awesome';
   content: '\f2bd'; /* 'user' icon */
   margin-right: 0.5em;
}

p.flag-adept {
  background-color: chartreuse;
}
p.flag-adept:before {
   font-family: 'Font Awesome';
   content: '\f19d'; /* 'graduation-cap' icon */
   margin-right: 0.5em;
}

details.flag-expert {
  background-color: lightsalmon;
}
details.flag-expert:before {
   font-family: 'Font Awesome';
   content: '\f5a2'; /* 'medal' icon */
   margin-right: 0.5em;
}
